cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its data, please cite it as
  below.
title: >-
  Runtime assurance monitor — prototype and falsification
  campaign
abstract: >-
  Executable prototype of an assurance monitor for an autonomous
  embedded decision layer, with an auditable decision-trace
  artefact, and a Monte Carlo campaign (600 runs, 15
  configurations) that falsifies the hypothesis that hardening on
  estimation uncertainty brings a safety benefit in the tested
  scenario. Negative result: the safety envelope alone reaches
  zero violations; every hardening variant costs availability.
